{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: none. The only data variable, `N`, is a context size and is not scored by a sampling statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the two parameter sampling statements so that `theta` is given its built-in prior before it is used in the prior for `y`. This preserves the same joint density because the original sampling statements contribute additively to the log density.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N; // Number of ys, supplied by interface
}

parameters {
  array[N] real y;  // Probabilistic variables y
  real theta; // Probabilistic variable theta
}

model {
  // Add marginal probabiltiy density for theta
  // to the joint log probability density using
  // equivalent sampling statement
  theta ~ normal(0, 1);

  // Add conditional probability density for the ys
  // given theta to the joint log probabilty density
  // using equivalent sampling statement
  y ~ normal(theta, 1);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N": 5}","protected_variables":[]}
